\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  O Jesus, King  most wonderful,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Thou Conqueror renowned,
\par Thou Sweetness most ineffable,
\par In whom all joys are found!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  When once Thou visitest the heart,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Then truth begins to shine,
\par Then earthly vanities depart,
\par Then kindles love divine.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  O Jesus, Light of all below,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Thou Fount of life and Light,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Surpassing all the joys we know,
\par And all we can desire, -
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4. May every heart confess Thy Name,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 And ever Thee adore,
\par And, seeking Thee, itself inflame
\par To seek Thee more and more.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Thee may our tongues for ever bless;
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Thee may we love alone,
\par And ever in our lives express
\par The image of Thine own.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

